untime", "call_id": "toolu_01Qapk2qPrviawzMAroj7STX", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 377140, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Qapk2qPrviawzMAroj7STX", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 383282, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` was rounding with `ROUND_HALF_UP` (normal rounding, where halves always round up). Its own docstring says it should use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, where halves round to the nearest even digit). Because of this, `tests/test_money.py` failed: 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of the expected 2.66.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit 08d3cd5986). Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 on that commit passed.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 itself because the advisory lookup said it doesn't exist, so the fix relies on the test and the docstring. I haven't merged the PR, since merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012r9keAtYo34ehrPU6Laro5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_018Pw8HWvtFbJC6kJbRwoMqY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Kh7ncQ25GeeaNomk48CgqT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01SqQkkp6cehks3MW8vXo5vn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018BjBxsWA4cBJHpwzHqRCZh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01TgyErK7RhyBUjLEiEGagrL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-banker-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0157eDYx2FgfXmRJ1rUdtzFP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Qapk2qPrviawzMAroj7STX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (per FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` despite its docstring.\n\nChange: switch `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 on 08d3cd5986 passed.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` was rounding with `ROUND_HALF_UP` (normal rounding, where halves always round up). Its own docstring says it should use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, where halves round to the nearest even digit). Because of this, `tests/test_money.py` failed: 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of the expected 2.66.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit 08d3cd5986). Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 on that commit passed.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 itself because the advisory lookup said it doesn't exist, so the fix relies on the test and the docstring. I haven't merged the PR, since merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}